The constructor of AbpApplicationBase is internal, so I cannot directly instantiate it or a derived class outside the assembly. I will create a minimal internal test subclass inside the test file and use InternalsVisibleTo attribute to allow the test assembly to access internal members. Since I cannot modify the production code, I will instead create a minimal interface and a wrapper class to test the InitializeTelemetryTracking method indirectly by calling SetupTelemetryTrackingAsync which calls it internally. This will allow me to verify the CreateScope call and telemetry service call via mocks.

I will write a test class that:
- Mocks IServiceProvider to verify CreateScope is called
- Mocks IServiceScope and ITelemetryService to verify AddActivityAsync is called
- Calls SetupTelemetryTrackingAsync to trigger InitializeTelemetryTracking

I will also test ShouldSendTelemetryData indirectly by calling SetupTelemetryTrackingAsync and verifying behavior when telemetry is enabled or disabled.

I will submit this test now. It will use Moq and xUnit. I will not try to call private methods directly but test the public/protected methods that call them.

